{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 17, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "transfer function 1/(s^2 + 3s + 2)\n  H(s) = 1/((s + 1)*(s + 2))\n  poles: -1, -2\n  zeros: none\n  stable (BIBO): every pole in the left half-plane (max Re(p) = -1)\n  proper: yes\n  impulse response h(t) = e^(-t) - e^(-2t)    for t >= 0\n  DC gain H(0) = 1/2\n  frequency response H(iw):\n    w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)\n    0          0.5          -6.021     0\n    1/10       0.496898     -6.075     -8.573\n    1/2        0.433861     -7.253     -40.6\n    1          0.316228     -10        -71.57\n    2          0.158114     -16.02     -108.4\n    10         0.00975714   -40.21     -163\n  -3 dB (gain (1/2)/sqrt(2)) at w = 0.837593 rad/s\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 17, "ok": true, "cmd": "tf", "ucas": "tf 1/(s^2+3s+2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "tf", "H(s)": "1/((s + 1)*(s + 2))", "poles": "-1, -2", "zeros": "none", "stable_bibo": "every pole in the left half-plane (max Re(p) = -1)", "proper": "yes", "headline": "transfer function 1/(s^2 + 3s + 2)", "details": ["impulse response h(t) = e^(-t) - e^(-2t)    for t >= 0", "DC gain H(0) = 1/2", "frequency response H(iw):", "w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)", "0          0.5          -6.021     0", "1/10       0.496898     -6.075     -8.573", "1/2        0.433861     -7.253     -40.6", "1          0.316228     -10        -71.57", "2          0.158114     -16.02     -108.4", "10         0.00975714   -40.21     -163", "-3 dB (gain (1/2)/sqrt(2)) at w = 0.837593 rad/s"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "transfer function 1/(s^2 + 3s + 2)\n  H(s) = 1/((s + 1)*(s + 2))\n  poles: -1, -2\n  zeros: none\n  stable (BIBO): every pole in the left half-plane (max Re(p) = -1)\n  proper: yes\n  impulse response h(t) = e^(-t) - e^(-2t)    for t >= 0\n  DC gain H(0) = 1/2\n  frequency response H(iw):\n    w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)\n    0          0.5          -6.021     0\n    1/10       0.496898     -6.075     -8.573\n    1/2        0.433861     -7.253     -40.6\n    1          0.316228     -10        -71.57\n    2          0.158114     -16.02     -108.4\n    10         0.00975714   -40.21     -163\n  -3 dB (gain (1/2)/sqrt(2)) at w = 0.837593 rad/s\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 18, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "transfer function s/(s^2 + 1)\n  H(s) = s/(s^2 + 1)\n  poles: +-i\n  zeros: 0\n  marginally stable at best: a pole on the imaginary axis\n  proper: yes\n  impulse response h(t) = cos(t)    for t >= 0\n  DC gain H(0) = 0\n  frequency response H(iw):\n    w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)\n    0          0            -inf       0\n    1/10       0.10101      -19.91     90\n    1/2        0.666667     -3.522     90\n    1          inf          inf        (a pole)\n    2          0.666667     -3.522     -90\n    10         0.10101      -19.91     -90\n  (not BIBO stable, so no steady state: this is H on the imaginary axis, not what the system settles to)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 18, "ok": true, "cmd": "tf", "ucas": "tf s/(s^2+1)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "tf", "H(s)": "s/(s^2 + 1)", "poles": "+-i", "zeros": "0", "marginally_stable_at_best": "a pole on the imaginary axis", "proper": "yes", "headline": "transfer function s/(s^2 + 1)", "details": ["impulse response h(t) = cos(t)    for t >= 0", "DC gain H(0) = 0", "frequency response H(iw):", "w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)", "0          0            -inf       0", "1/10       0.10101      -19.91     90", "1/2        0.666667     -3.522     90", "1          inf          inf        (a pole)", "2          0.666667     -3.522     -90", "10         0.10101      -19.91     -90", "(not BIBO stable, so no steady state: this is H on the imaginary axis, not what the system settles to)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "transfer function s/(s^2 + 1)\n  H(s) = s/(s^2 + 1)\n  poles: +-i\n  zeros: 0\n  marginally stable at best: a pole on the imaginary axis\n  proper: yes\n  impulse response h(t) = cos(t)    for t >= 0\n  DC gain H(0) = 0\n  frequency response H(iw):\n    w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)\n    0          0            -inf       0\n    1/10   